For manual (copying) USB install UEFI-boot, copy the folders EFI, boot, live, and the file grub.cfg to the root (/) of a FAT32 formatted partition, e.g. /mnt/sdb1.
And it should boot, no bootloader install stuff required.

Secure Boot: the build replaces the grub in EFI/boot with Debian's signed one
(and refreshes shim and MokManager) when it can reach the Debian archive, so
the ISO and a USB stick made from it boot with Secure Boot on and nothing to
enrol. The files shipped in this directory are the fallback for a build made
without network; with those, Secure Boot needs puppy.cer enrolled through
MokManager on first boot. Either way, for a hand-made USB stick copy EFI, boot
and live to the root of the FAT32 partition as before.
